ox":[0,1277,1405,239]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"9dd0857cf6596def0935-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process find an orthonormal basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ from the set of vectors $\\{(1,1,2),(1,-1,2),(1,0,1)\\}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-8-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1507,1405,151]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"9dd0857cf6596def0935-q-8","number":"3B","markdown":"Solve $(5x^4 + 3x^2y^2 - 2xy^3)\\,dx + (2x^3y - 3x^2y^2 - 5y^4)\\,dy = 0$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-9-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1650,1405,76]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"9dd0857cf6596def0935-q-9","number":"3C","markdown":"Solve\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} - 2\\dfrac{dy}{dx} + y = e^x\\sin x\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-10-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1718,1405,87]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"9dd0857cf6596def0935-q-10","number":"4A","markdown":"Prove that in a vector space $V$ over a field $F$, every maximal linearly independent set of vectors forms a basis for $V$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-11-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1797,1405,42]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"9dd0857cf6596def0935-q-11","number":"4B","markdown":"Solve \n\n$$\nx^2y'' - xy' + 2y = x\\sin(\\log x)\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1,2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-12-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1831,1405,49]},{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/9dd0857cf6596def0935/q-12-p-2-continuation.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,79,1405,254]}],"confidence":"low","reviewNotes":["The source contains a possible continuation on another page. I